    "text": "A conical pendulum of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis and moves in a circle in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> plane. The radius of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and its center is vertically below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>. The speed of the pendulum, in its circular path, will be - <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/af1f5f5c-c17d-4e6a-9fc0-9c0863393cf8-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 167px;\" />",
